// A NULLARY function symbol inside a SAPIC conditional, end to end.
//
// A nullary application is neither a literal nor a parenthesised call: HS
// `prettyTerm` matches `FApp (NoEq (f, _)) []` before the general `ppFun` case
// and prints the bare name (Term/Term.hs:314), so `nil` carries no `()`.  A
// condition is a FORMULA, so `prettySapicComb (Cond a)` renders it with
// `prettySyntacticSapicFormula` (Theory/Sapic/Process.hs:476) rather than the
// term printer a `let` right-hand side uses, and everything the translation
// derives from the step reads off that one rendering:
//
//   - the rule name, `filter isAlpha` over `prettySapicTopLevel`
//     (HS `toRule`, Sapic/Facts.hs:384,401), so the bare `nil` contributes its
//     three letters and the names end `…nilk_0_1` / `…nilk_1_1`.  A
//     parenthesised or dropped nullary spells them otherwise, and the
//     restriction names are `Restr_` ++ the rule name;
//   - the `process=` rule attribute, which reprints the whole condition;
//   - the `Restr_…` action fact carrying the condition's terms, which appears
//     inside the `variants (modulo AC)` block too — `'g'^k` is there to force
//     that block, so `nil` is re-rendered under a substitution as well.
//
// `add/2 [AC]` puts a user-AC operand beside the nullary one in the same
// tuple, so the nullary rides through the AC flatten-and-sort path rather than
// only the verbatim one, and `nil/0` also pins the arity-0 entry of the
// `functions:` signature echo.  The `then` and `else` sides mint two
// restrictions from the one condition, so both carry the term.
//
// No corpus theory declares a nullary function symbol inside a SAPIC process.
//
// Compared slice: the whole `theory … end` echo (see check.sh).

theory SapicNullaryCond
begin

builtins: diffie-hellman
functions: add/2 [AC], nil/0

predicates: Eq(a, b) <=> a = b

process:
  in(k);
  if Eq(<'g'^k, add(k,'a'), nil>, k) then
    out('yes')
  else
    out('no')

end
